. 
. 
. *******************************************************************
. * Robustness tests
. *******************************************************************
. 
. *******************************************************************
. * a. Children measured in all three waves
. *******************************************************************
. 
. * IMPORTANT NOTE IS THIS IS JUST A ROBUSTNESS CHECK, IT DROPS THE SAMPLE SIZE
>  SIGNIFICANTLY 
. 
. * We run the same event study as above but only children measured in all thre
> e waves with the outcome nonmissing in each. This way the 2002 lead and the 2
> 009 coefficient come from the same children
. foreach v in haz waz bmiz {
  2.         * Here we count each childs rows to make sure they are in all thre
> e waves. This is done by generating a flag column called "all3" for children 
> seen in all 3 waves. First we count the total that are not missing in each ro
> w, then we flag the row if not missing and the child present in all 3 rows.
.     bysort pid_link_canonical: egen n3_`v' = total(e_`v' == 1 & !missing(`v')
> )
  3.     gen e_`v'_all3 = (e_`v' == 1 & !missing(`v') & n3_`v' == 3)
  4.     label variable e_`v'_all3 "Event study sample, children in all 3 waves
> , `v'"
  5. }

. 
. 
. * Now we do the regressions again looking at just kids in all three waves
. foreach v in haz waz bmiz {
  2.     * Model 1: Basic DID
.     reghdfe `v' treat_post if s_`v' == 1 & e_`v'_all3 == 1, absorb($FE_month)
>  vce(cluster cvegeo05)
  3.     * Model 2: DID controlling for the other droughts in the window
.     reghdfe `v' treat_post $did_controls if s_`v' == 1 & e_`v'_all3 == 1, abs
> orb($FE_month) vce(cluster cvegeo05)
  4.     * Model 3: DID with baseline 2002 household controls and 2005 child an
> d mother controls
.     reghdfe `v' treat_post $did_controls $controls02 $controls05 if s_`v' == 
> 1 & e_`v'_all3 == 1, absorb($FE_month) vce(cluster cvegeo05)
  5.     * Model 4: Model 3 with the father and birth controls, smaller sample
.     reghdfe `v' treat_post $did_controls $controls02 $controls05 $controls05_
> birth if s_`v' == 1 & e_`v'_all3 == 1, absorb($FE_month) vce(cluster cvegeo05
> )
  6.     * Model 5: Triple difference, does 2002 remittance receipt buffer the 
> drought
.     reghdfe `v' treat_post remittance_hh_02_post treat_post_remit02 $did_cont
> rols $controls02 $controls05 if s_`v' == 1 & e_`v'_all3 == 1, absorb($FE_mont
> h) vce(cluster cvegeo05)
  7.     * Total drought effect for children in 2002 remittance households
.     lincom treat_post + treat_post_remit02
  8. }
